Title: SAI STM32U585

Body:
**Describe the set-up**

STM32U585 custom board
Visual Studio Code with zephyr

**Describe the problem**

To use the SAI-Block in Zephyr with the device tree the current stm32u585xx.h (https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/hal_stm32/blob/main/stm32cube/stm32u5xx/soc/stm32u585xx.h) does not work (for me?) when I add two separated SAI blocks to the device tree.
In my project I fixed it with the changes in this PR to only add one complete SAI: https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/hal_stm32/pull/248/files

With that changes I can add the SAI the following way:
i2s2: i2s@40015800 {
			compatible = "st,stm32u5-i2s";
			reg = <0x40015800 0x400>;
			interrupts = <91 0>;
			#address-cells = <1>;
			#size-cells = <0>;
			clocks = <&rcc STM32_CLOCK_BUS_APB2 0x00400000>,
				 <&rcc STM32_SRC_PLL2_P SAI2_SEL(0)>;
			dmas = <&gpdma1 1 39 (STM32_DMA_PERIPH_TX | STM32_DMA_PRIORITY_HIGH | STM32_DMA_MEM_16BITS | STM32_DMA_PERIPH_16BITS)
				&gpdma1 0 38 (STM32_DMA_PERIPH_RX | STM32_DMA_PRIORITY_HIGH | STM32_DMA_MEM_16BITS | STM32_DMA_PERIPH_16BITS)>;
			dma-names = "tx", "rx";
			status = "disabled";
		};

